# Worktrees the review subagent runs in (isolation: "worktree"). Ignored
# in the bridge since Cycle 108 and not here, which left them one
# `git add -A` away from being committed by the cycle under review.
.claude/

# Scratch from the digest roll in `prompt.md` step 7, which tells a cycle
# to `cd` into this repo and write `live.md`/`archive.md` here before
# calling `tools.roll_digest`. They are fragments of Edvard's
# `journal-digest.md`, not source, and they have been swept into a commit
# by `git add -A` twice: Cycle 125 caught it before merging, Cycle 132
# did not, and #111 shipped both files to `main`. Ignoring them is the
# only version of this fix that does not depend on the next cycle
# remembering.
/live.md
/live2.md
/archive.md

# Every other scratch file `prompt.md` tells a cycle to write into this
# repo root, for exactly the reason above. The digest roll got its three
# ignored after being committed twice; the claim ledger (step 2) and the
# retro ledger (step 2's Friday block) were left out and `claims.json`
# was then committed twice more -- deleted once in 084fbd6, and again by
# Cycle 194, whose reviewer caught it in the PR. The list, not the habit,
# is what stops this: any `get > <name>` in `prompt.md` that lands here
# belongs in this file the day it is written.
/claims.json
/claims2.json
/ledger.json
/iss.md
